name 'thinking-critically-about-ai-preassessment-q15_2026-pilot_2026'

question 'A student is working on a math problem they have never seen before. They want to learn how to solve it. Which approach best demonstrates good judgment about when to use AI?'

wrong 'Immediately ask AI for the full solution so the problem is finished quickly.'
wrong 'Never use AI at all, because using AI for schoolwork is always cheating.'
right 'Attempt the problem independently first, then use AI to check their reasoning or get a hint if stuck, rather than to replace their own thinking.'
wrong 'Ask AI to explain an entirely different, easier problem so they never have to struggle.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

